Z||000000||84Bill||09-13-2001||03:09 PM||||Apparently we are going to fight this foe <A HREF="http://www.msnbc.com/news/627028_asp.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.msnbc.com/news/627028_asp.htm</A> <P>WHEN YOU look at the list of candidates, one resides in the region,” Secretary of State Colin Powell told a news conference.<BR>       Asked whether he was referring to bin Laden, Powell replied: “Yes.”<BR>       Earlier, the president told reporters at the White House, <B>“We have just seen the first war of the 21st century.”</B><BR>       Allies around the world, he added, have vowed to help us “whip terrorism.”<BR>       “This is now the focus of my administration ... <B>now that war has been declared,” Bush said.</B><BR>       The president’s eyes were red and wet as he ended his comments, his head and hands trembling slightly as he closed with, “This is a terrible moment but this country will not relent until we have saved ourselves and others from the terrible tragedy that came upon America.”<BR>||||reg||4
